	)
	(text "GPIO MAP (pin = QFN-80 pin)\nGPIO0    77  FLASH_CS1    QMI CS1n, log flash select\nGPIO1    78  ADXL_INT1  ADXL375 INT1\nGPIO2    79  ADXL_SCK      SPI0 SCK\nGPIO3    80  ADXL_MOSI     SPI0 TX\nGPIO4     1  ADXL_MISO     SPI0 RX\nGPIO5     2  PWM8         PWM2 B -> J6 row 10 (S8)\nGPIO6     3  ICM_INT1  ICM-45686 INT1\nGPIO7     4  ICM_CS  ICM-45686 CS\nGPIO8     6  ICM_MISO  SPI1 RX\nGPIO9     7  BARO_SCL      I2C0 SCL\nGPIO10    8  ICM_SCK  SPI1 SCK\nGPIO11    9  ICM_MOSI  SPI1 TX\nGPIO12   11  BARO_SDA      I2C0 SDA\nGPIO13   12  BARO_INT     BMP581 INT\nGPIO14   13  ADXL_CS       ADXL375 CS\nGPIO15   14  PWM7         PWM7 B -> J6 row 9 (S7)\nGPIO16   16  ELRS_RX      UART0 TX -> radio RX\nGPIO17   17  ELRS_TX      UART0 RX <- radio TX\nGPIO18   18  ICM_INT2      ICM-45686 INT2\nGPIO19   19  PWM6         PWM1 B -> J6 row 8 (S6)\nGPIO20   20  PWM5         PWM2 A -> J6 row 7 (S5)\nGPIO21   21  ADXL_INT2     ADXL375 INT2\nGPIO22   22  MAG_SDA      I2C1 SDA\nGPIO23   23  MAG_SCL      I2C1 SCL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "2107c554-d365-573a-9cfb-23e5a778a93a")
	)
	(text "PORT NAMING: a port label is named for the peripheral pin it comes from, so GPS_TX / ELRS_TX are module outputs\nand land on MCU UART RX pins, while GPS_RX / ELRS_RX are module inputs fed by the MCU UART TX pins. On the IO\narray (POWER 3) the UART rows are therefore 1 GPS_RX (silk T0) / 2 GPS_TX (R0) / 3 ELRS_RX (T1) / 4 ELRS_TX (R1),\nrows 5/6 are MAG_SDA / MAG_SCL, rows 7-10 the PWM5-8 servo signals and rows 11-14 the four exposed spares.\nThe array is three stacked 1x14 rows: J6 SIGNAL, J7 POWER, J8 GND. All array SIGNAL pins are 3.3 V CMOS.\nGPIO37 (pin 46) is SPARE and unconnected again: it used to read PWR_SRC_ST, the open-drain status output of\nthe U25 TPS2121 mux, and the mux is gone. USB presence is already readable on the VBUS_SENSE divider (GPIO40)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140 240.243 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "27eb724b-54bb-52d9-8a07-f1658d5b65fa")
	)
	(text "I2C1 pull-ups"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 355.6 140.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "37a71e6b-8b76-567c-adab-6a99df48e4d9")
	)
	(text "BOARD 1 - RP2354B, QFN-80, 2 MB IN-PACKAGE QSPI FLASH.  Digital rails on V3V3_SYS, core DVDD\nfrom the on-chip buck.  Supply pins fan out on the left into one decoupling group per rail."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 10 7 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "3f8528ce-df8d-5b98-9247-6e30201a64c2")
	)
	(text "SPARE IO: GPIO44-47 remain on IO block J6 rows 11-14.\nGPIO26, GPIO27 and GPIO35 are unexposed and carry no-connect flags.\nGPIO budget: 41 assigned, 4 exposed spares, 3 unconnected.\nSPI0: ADXL375 only. SPI1: ICM-45686 only. I2C0: BMP581 only.\nNative SD: GPIO28-33, PIO + DMA (window 16-47). Independent sensor interrupts.\nSee PINOUT.md for the complete allocation."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140 254.922 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "4a06ca06-1372-5348-80a0-994102a71279")
	)
	(text "  (pins 68+69 share it).\nVREG_AVDD RC = 33 ohm + 4.7 uF (design guide Sec 2.1), taken from V3V3_SYS; VREG_FB is tied to DVDD, VREG_PGND to GND,\n  EP to GND."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 265 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "59d32cce-0fca-5a61-9e43-aeb13b88be44")
	)
	(text "SD source-series damping\nR58: place next to U20 GPIO32 (pin 40).\n22 ohm nominal; tune 0-33 ohm.\nNo pull resistor on SD_CLK."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 302.26 207.01 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7e9d38a3-cc71-46ad-bf31-5b17a15c1aef")
	)
	(text "Reset and BOOTSEL"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 168.91 140.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8ef3747b-9f37-59af-9024-ad0f49013a02")
	)
	(text "12 MHz crystal"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 152.4 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "9766288b-8f91-5fbb-903d-c00a10b60fd6")
	)
	(text "\nGPIO24   25  GPS_RX       UART1 TX -> GPS RX\nGPIO25   26  GPS_TX       UART1 RX <- GPS TX\nGPIO26   27  (no connect)  unexposed spare - no connect\nGPIO27   28  (no connect)  unexposed spare - no connect\nGPIO28   36  SD_DAT0  native SD DAT0\nGPIO29   37  SD_DAT1  native SD DAT1\nGPIO30   38  SD_DAT2  native SD DAT2\nGPIO31   39  SD_DAT3  native SD DAT3\nGPIO32   40  SD_CLK_MCU    PIO native SD clock -> R58 22R -> SD_CLK (window 16-47)\nGPIO33   42  SD_CMD        PIO native SD command (window 16-47)\nGPIO34   43  ESC_TELEM_RX ESC KISS telemetry in (PIO UART RX, window 16-47), 1k series R54\nGPIO35   44  (no connect)  unexposed spare - no connect\nGPIO36   45  PWM4         DShot via PIO (window 16-47)\nGPIO37   46  PWM3         DShot via PIO (window 16-47)\nGPIO38   47  PWM2         DShot via PIO (window 16-47)\nGPIO39   48  PWM1         DShot via PIO (window 16-47)\nGPIO40   49  VBUS_SENSE   ADC0, USB_VBUS 10k/15k divider\nGPIO41   52  CURR_SENSE   ADC1, ESC current sense, 1k + 100n\nGPIO42   53  VBAT_SENSE   ADC2, VBAT 100k/10k divider, 36.3 V FS\nGPIO43   54  LED_DATA      WS2812 data -> R55 (PIO, window 16-47)\nGPIO44   55  IO_GPIO44    ADC4 -> J6 row 11 (A44)\nGPIO45   56  IO_GPIO45    ADC5 -> J6 row 12 (A45)\nGPIO46   57  IO_GPIO46    ADC6 -> J6 row 13 (A46)\nGPIO47   58  IO_GPIO47    ADC7 -> J6 row 14 (A47)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 63.5 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 0.85 0.85)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b561fdf6-aab7-5065-98d1-bdf4a4434d67")
	)
	(text "RP2354B, QFN-80, 2 MB in-package QSPI flash. Digital rails on V3V3_SYS, core DVDD from the on-chip buck.\nRAIL SPLIT: V3V3_ANA (TPS7A20 LDO) now feeds exactly one RP2354B pin - ADC_AVDD (pin 59, with C40). The core regulator\n  input\nfilter R20/C41 that produces VREG_AVDD is fed from V3V3_SYS instead, so the buck-converter reference current no longer\n  flows out\nof the low-noise analog rail and the sensors do not share a rail with it; V3V3_ANA is left carrying only ADC_AVDD and\n  the MEMS.\nDecoupling, core regulator, crystal and BOOTSEL follow the RP2350 hardware design guide; every pin net is a global\n  label."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140 222 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "c69e7eb4-ed0a-5222-9667-fdb7789cc5b4")
	)
	(text "Crystal circuit per design guide Sec 4. Y1 IS TAXM12M4RFBCCT2T (LCSC C133337), 12 MHz, SMD 3225 4-pad, CL = 12 pF -\n  the\nABM8-272-T3 the earlier revision named is not orderable at JLCPCB in any form (reports/jlc-audit.md section 1).\nLOAD CAPS FOLLOW THE CRYSTAL, NOT THE OTHER WAY ROUND: CL = C46*C47/(C46+C47) + Cstray, so C46/C47 are 18 pF C0G each\n(2 x 18 pF in series = 9 pF, plus ~3 pF of XIN/XTAL_DRV pin and trace stray = 12 pF, matching CL exactly). They were\n15 pF against the old CL 10 pF part; leaving 15 pF on a CL 12 pF crystal gives 10.5 pF of load, i.e. an under-loaded\noscillator running fast by roughly the trim sensitivity of the part. The ~3 pF stray is the design-guide estimate and\n  is\nthe one term here that is not a datasheet number - if the board is ever pulled for frequency, that is the term to\n  measure.\n1 k in the XOUT leg to limit drive with a 50 ohm ESR crystal. C38 is the single design-guide decoupling exception"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 140 271.383 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.1 1.1)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cae83ad4-6775-51bc-9c00-88c283d4c51f")
	)
